Host-side OTA sub-element parser regression tests
================================================

Run from the project root (requires g++):

    mkdir -p .pio
    g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fsanitize=address,undefined -g test/ota_element_parser_test.cpp -o .pio/ota_element_parser_test
    .pio/ota_element_parser_test

Tests cover all 512 block partitions of a small OTA sub-element, including
fragmented and header-only blocks, malformed tags/lengths, null payloads,
changing total sizes, oversized payloads, incomplete transfers, and parser reset.
These tests are standalone host tests, not ESP-IDF/PlatformIO device tests.

Hardware checks still needed:
- Flood commands across all four endpoints; confirm the final states match and
  Zigbee stays responsive. Intermediate states may coalesce under load.
- Observe relay GPIOs during power-up/reset; verify external pull-ups keep
  active-low inputs OFF before firmware takes control.
- Abort OTA downloads repeatedly and retry; confirm stable free heap and a
  successful subsequent update.
- Query a server without a newer image; confirm no false availability log.
